{"name":"New Brick Red","hex":"#cb4154","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"new","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Newar."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Recently made, or created.","Of recent origin; having taken place recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new"},{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of red","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color red may differ in hue, chroma, lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a red or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Shades_of_Red.svg/330px-Shades_of_Red.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_red","wikidata":"Q7460345"},{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/RGB_illumination.jpg/330px-RGB_illumination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/RGB_illumination.jpg/330px-RGB_illumination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARGB_illumination.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Twenty_hues_of_the_Munsell_color_system_at_maximum_chroma.png/500px-Twenty_hues_of_the_Munsell_color_system_at_maximum_chroma.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, htt